  "notes": {
    "heritage": "The 4A-GE is Toyota's legendary high-revving naturally aspirated engine. Made famous by the AE86 Corolla (star of Initial D), it represents Toyota's commitment to driver engagement. The engine evolved through five generations, culminating in the 165HP 20V Blacktop.",
    "reputation": "A true enthusiast engine - designed to rev and reward skilled driving. The 4AGE responds exceptionally well to modifications despite its small displacement. The 20V versions with individual throttle bodies are particularly prized.",
    "common_issues": [
      "Oil consumption on high-mileage engines",
      "Timing belt critical (interference engine)",
      "Distributor failures on 16V versions",
      "Water pump and thermostat failures",
      "Head gasket failures if overheated",
      "Rod bearings wear on high-mileage/abused engines"
    ],
    "strengths": [
      "Loves to rev - designed for high RPM",
      "Lightweight compact design",
      "Excellent throttle response",
      "Strong aftermarket support",
      "20V versions with ITBs are exceptional",
      "Robust iron block",
      "Great for track and autocross"
    ],
    "maintenance_critical": [
      "Timing belt every 60,000 miles (CRITICAL - interference engine)",
      "Valve adjustment every 60,000 miles (16V - 20V have hydraulic lifters)",
      "Oil changes every 3,000 miles (high-revving usage)",
      "Spark plugs every 20,000 miles"
    ],
    "cultural_significance": "The AE86 with its 4A-GE engine became a cultural icon through Initial D anime/manga. It established the template for the affordable, lightweight, RWD sports car that Toyota later revived with the GT86/GR86.",
